 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "One-variable fields over a separably closed field",
 "statement": "If $F$ is separably closed, then\n$\\operatorname{cd}_{\\rm tor}(F(x))\\leq1$, with the bound of\n[def-sc-etale-torsion-cd].",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sf-cbc/lem-sc-one-variable-field-cd.md",
  "place": "node lem-sc-one-variable-field-cd, order 1549"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sc-etale-torsion-cd"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The field $F(x)$ is the filtered union of\n$F[x,1/h]$, for nonzero $h\\in F[x]$.\nEach corresponding scheme is an affine curve.\nThe algebraic closure $\\overline F/F$ is purely inseparable,\nso its base change preserves the etale topos by\n[thm-weil-pbc-universal-homeomorphism-invariance].\nOver $\\overline F$ the bound is one by\n[lem-sc-arbitrary-curve-cd].\nUse [lem-sc-cd-affine-limit] to pass to the fraction field.",
   "uses": [
    "thm-weil-pbc-universal-homeomorphism-invariance",
    "lem-sc-arbitrary-curve-cd",
    "lem-sc-cd-affine-limit"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
